1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,610
Good morning. Total Insurance. Judy speaking, how may I help you?

2
00:00:03,610 --> 00:00:07,836
I recently shipped my belongings from overseas back here to Australia

3
00:00:07,836 --> 00:00:10,910
and I took out insurance with your company.

4
00:00:10,910 --> 00:00:15,230
Some items were damaged during the move so I need to make a claim.

5
00:00:15,230 --> 00:00:16,330
What do I have to do?

6
00:00:16,330 --> 00:00:20,250
Okay, well first I need to get a few details about this.

7
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:22,420
Can you give me your name please?

8
00:00:22,420 --> 00:00:25,110
Yes. It's Michael Alexander.

9
00:00:25,110 --> 00:00:28,060
Okay. And your address please?

10
00:00:28,060 --> 00:00:30,560
My old address or my current one?

11
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:31,670
Your current one.

12
00:00:31,670 --> 00:00:36,610
It's 24 Manly Street, Milperra near Sydney.

13
00:00:36,610 --> 00:00:38,550
What was the suburb, sorry?

14
00:00:38,550 --> 00:00:44,420
Milperra. M. I-L-P-E-R-R-A.

15
00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:48,460
Right. Now, who was the shipping agent Mr Alexander?

16
00:00:48,460 --> 00:00:51,200
You mean the company we used?

17
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:54,800
Yes, the company who packed everything up at the point of origin.

18
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:59,720
Oh, it was, er... First Class Movers.

19
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:03,860
Okay... where were the goods shipped from?

20
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:09,640
China, but the ship came via Singapore and was there for about a week.

21
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:13,330
Don't worry, all of that information will be in the documentation.

22
00:01:13,330 --> 00:01:17,170
Now, the dates. Do you know when the ship arrived?

23
00:01:17,170 --> 00:01:22,490
It left on the 11th of October and got to Sydney on the 28th of November.

24
00:01:22,490 --> 00:01:27,220
Okay. I need one more thing. There's a reference number.

25
00:01:27,220 --> 00:01:31,470
It should be in the top right-hand corner of the pink form they gave you.

26
00:01:31,470 --> 00:01:41,940
Let me have a look. I have so many papers. Yes, here it is. It's 601 ACK.

27
00:01:41,940 --> 00:01:42,710
Thanks.

28
00:01:42,710 --> 00:01:49,470
I need to take down a few details of the actual damage over the phone before you put in a full report.

29
00:01:49,470 --> 00:01:53,460
Can you tell me how many items were damaged and what the damage was?

30
00:01:53,460 --> 00:01:57,800
Yes, well four things actually. I'll start with the big things.

31
00:01:57,800 --> 00:02:02,370
My TV first of all. It's a large one, very expensive.

32
00:02:02,370 --> 00:02:05,320
Our insurance doesn't cover electrical problems.

33
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:07,040
It isn't an electrical problem.

34
00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:10,070
The screen has a huge crack in it so it's unusable.

35
00:02:10,070 --> 00:02:14,070
I see. Any idea of the price to repair it?

36
00:02:14,070 --> 00:02:18,470
No. Well, I don't think it can be repaired. It will need a new one.

37
00:02:18,470 --> 00:02:22,340
Okay. I'll make a note of that and we'll see what we can do

38
00:02:22,820 --> 00:02:24,670
Now, what was the second item?

39
00:02:24,670 --> 00:02:28,490
The cabinet from the bathroom was damaged as well.

40
00:02:28,490 --> 00:02:31,650
It's a lovely cabinet, we use it to keep our towels in.

41
00:02:31,650 --> 00:02:33,700
And what is the extent of the damage?

42
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:38,920
Well, the back and the sides seem okay but the door has a huge hole in it.

43
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:42,460
It can't be repaired. I'm really not very happy about it.

44
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:44,840
And how much do you think it will cost to replace it?

45
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:50,300
Well, when I bought it last year I paid $125 for it.

46
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:56,550
But the one I've seen here in Sydney is a bit more expensive, it's $140.

47
00:02:56,550 --> 00:02:58,760
Right, and what was the third item?

48
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:03,300
My dining room table. It's a lovely table from Indonesia.

49
00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:06,280
It must have been very hot inside the container

50
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:09,700
because one leg has completely split down the middle.

51
00:03:09,700 --> 00:03:13,600
The top and the other three look okay thank goodness

52
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:15,930
Any idea of the price to repair it?

53
00:03:15,930 --> 00:03:18,740
Well, I had an estimate done on this actually

54
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:21,100
because it is a very special table to us.

55
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:25,860
They quoted us $200, which is really pricey

56
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:28,550
so I hope the insurance will cover the total cost.

57
00:03:28,550 --> 00:03:32,720
I'm sure that will be fine. What was the last item, Mr Alexander?

58
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:37,080
Well, we have a lovely set of china plates and dishes

59
00:03:37,220 --> 00:03:39,620
you know, with matching cups, saucers, the lot.

60
00:03:39,620 --> 00:03:43,420
They were all in the one box which must have got dropped

61
00:03:43,420 --> 00:03:46,600
because some plates were broken - six actually.

62
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:49,350
And can you tell me the replacement value of these?

63
00:03:49,350 --> 00:03:50,656
Well, it's hard to say

64
00:03:50,656 --> 00:03:52,320
because they were part of a set

65
00:03:52,860 --> 00:03:56,140
but they can be up to $10 each as it's such a good set.

66
00:03:56,140 --> 00:03:59,500
Okay, so that would be around $60 altogether?

67
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:00,760
Yes, that's right.

68
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:02,700
And is that all of the items?

69
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:06,080
Yes. So what do I have to do now?
